import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../data/schema';
---
<Site
  title="Why I built Just Sign It"
  description="I needed to sign a few documents for my township and couldn't find a simple PDF signer that didn't make me create an account. So I built one."
  schema={breadcrumbSchema(Astro.site, 'Why I built this', '/why')}
>
  <h1>Why I built this</h1>
  <p>I recently had to sign a few documents for my township. Simple stuff: open the PDF, put my signature on it, send it back.</p>
  <p>Ten minutes and four failed attempts later, I still hadn’t found an online PDF signer that just let me do that. Every one of them wanted me to create an account, start a free trial, or jump through a thousand hoops before I could sign a single page.</p>
  <p>I realized it doesn’t need to be that way. <mark>Signing a PDF should take less than a minute.</mark> So I built Just Sign It.</p>

  <h2>What I wanted</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No account.</strong> Open the page, sign the PDF, download it. Done.</li>
    <li><strong>No uploading.</strong> Documents like these are private, so everything happens in your browser and your file never leaves your computer.</li>
    <li><strong>No catch.</strong> It’s free, and the code is open source on <a href="https://github.com/john-rock/just-sign-it">GitHub</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>If you’ve got a PDF to sign, I hope this saves you the ten minutes it cost me.</p>
  <p class="cta"><a href="/sign" class="btn primary">Sign a PDF</a></p>
</Site>
